  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>tr_fact_sales - loads mart_fact_sales, one row per order line; safe to run again.
Connection: MySQL:sampledata (localhost, pentaho_admin). Run fact_sales.sql first, and load the three
dimensions.

1. csvi-order_lines: CSV file input, reads ORDER_FILE (January 2003 to April 2005 by default).
2. dbl-dim_date: Database lookup, the whole table cached, the_date to date_key, default 0.
3. dlu-customer_key: Dimension lookup/update with Update the dimension? cleared; the version
of customer_number valid on order_date.
4. dbl-dim_product: Database lookup, the whole table cached, product_code to product_key.
5. calc-sales_amount: Calculator, price_each * quantity_ordered (the BigNumber first, to keep the cents).
6. iu-fact_sales: Insert / Update keyed on order_number and order_line_number.

Shipped data: 2,867 order lines, 10,161,912.81 in sales; the same after a second run.</note>
      <xloc>96</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>610</width>
      <heigth>242</heigth>
